course: dictionary
lesson: 1427
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «The carnival came to town on Saturday, with rides and a candy floss stall.» Here carnival means a fair, because rides and stalls are the clues.
explain: The same word can mean something else in a different sentence. «The carnival in Rio had music, dancing and bright costumes.» Now carnival means a big street party, because music, dancing and costumes are the clues. Always ask: which meaning fits the clues around the word?
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense. A fair fits «We queued for the carnival ride», but not «We danced in the carnival ride». If the sentence stops making sense, try the other meaning.
fact: Carnival is a noun. Its plural is carnivals.
fact: «Carnival» can mean a fair with rides, games and food that often travels from town to town.
fact: «Carnival» can also mean a big street party with music, dancing and costumes, like the Notting Hill Carnival.
fact: «Mardi gras» means "fat Tuesday", and it was the last day for rich food before Lent.
fact: Phrases such as «carnival ride», «carnival games» and «school carnival» usually show the fair meaning.
exercise: «The school carnival had a ride on the big wheel and a tombola.» What is a carnival here? | A long train journey | *A fair with rides and games | A lesson about fractions | A quiet walk in the woods
exercise: «Everyone wore masks and costumes at the carnival, and the band played all afternoon.» What kind of carnival is this? | A quiet picnic in the park | *A big street party with music and dancing | A school spelling test | A travelling fair with a ghost train
exercise: Nadia says «Mardi gras» means "fat Tuesday". Why was it a special day? | It was the day everyone went swimming | It was the day the fair packed up and left town | *It was the last day for rich food before Lent | It was the first day of the school holidays
test: «Each carnival ride costs 3 tickets. Maya has 12 tickets.» How many rides can she go on? | *4 | 3 | 5 | 9
test: Which clue in a sentence tells you carnival means a street party? | Tickets and prizes | Rides and candy floss | Stalls and games | *Costumes and dancing
exam: «The carnival in Rio has music, dancing and costumes.» What kind of carnival is this? | A school sports day | A travelling fair with rides | A market selling fish | *A big street party
